---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: login">
  <p class="demo-note">
    An authentication entry screen — the one screen every ERP app has and the one
    where getting the details wrong locks real users out. Composed entirely from
    existing components, zero new CSS: <code>.bo-widget</code> (the card primitive)
    centers the form on the canvas, fields are plain <code>.bo-form-field</code>s
    with the <strong>correct <code>autocomplete</code> tokens</strong>
    (<code>username</code> / <code>current-password</code> — this is what lets
    password managers fill the form), and errors use the same
    <a href={base + '/patterns/validation-summary'}>validation-summary pattern</a> as any
    other form. Try it: submit the empty form.
  </p>

  <section class="demo" style="background: var(--bo-color-bg-canvas); padding: var(--bo-space-8) var(--bo-space-4)">
    <div class="bo-widget" style="inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 24rem; margin-inline: auto">
      <div class="bo-widget__header">
        <span class="bo-widget__title">Sign in to busy-office</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-widget__body">
        <form data-validation-summary novalidate hx-boost="false" class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight">
          <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
            <p><strong>There is a problem</strong></p>
            <ul></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="login-user">Email or username</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="login-user" name="username" autocomplete="username" required />
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="login-pass">Password</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="login-pass" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" required />
          </div>
          <label class="bo-choice"><input type="checkbox" class="bo-checkbox" name="remember" /> Keep me signed in</label>
          <div class="bo-form-actions">
            <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Sign in</button>
            <a href="#" class="bo-u-text-muted">Forgot password?</a>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initValidationSummary } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initValidationSummary();
  </script>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The details that matter on a login screen</h2>
    <ul class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight" style="padding-inline-start: 1.25rem">
      <li><strong><code>autocomplete="username"</code> / <code>"current-password"</code></strong> —
      the standardized tokens password managers key on. Omitting them (or using
      <code>off</code>) breaks credential autofill, which hurts the users who rely
      on managers for strong unique passwords.</li>
      <li><strong>Server-error recovery uses the same summary box</strong> — on a
      failed sign-in your server re-renders the form with the
      <code>data-validation-summary-box</code> alert visible and a message like
      "The email or password you entered is incorrect." Say which <em>action</em>
      failed, never which field was wrong (that's credential enumeration).</li>
      <li><strong>No premature lockout messaging</strong> — if you rate-limit or
      lock accounts, tell the user how to recover ("try again in 15 minutes" /
      "reset your password"), in the same alert, as text — not a dead end.</li>
      <li><strong>The password field never blocks paste</strong> — paste-blocking
      breaks password managers; nothing here does it and nothing should.</li>
      <li><strong>One column, one card</strong> — <code>.bo-widget</code> with
      <code>max-inline-size</code> centered on the canvas; no new "login layout"
      CSS exists because none is needed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{`<!-- inline-size: 100% matters: .bo-widget is a size container
     (container-type: inline-size), so outside a .bo-widget-grid it needs an
     explicit width — max-inline-size alone collapses it. -->
<div class="bo-widget" style="inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 24rem; margin-inline: auto">
  <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">Sign in</span></div>
  <div class="bo-widget__body">
    <form method="post" action="/session" data-validation-summary class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight">
      <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
        <p>There is a problem</p>
        <ul></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-field">
        <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="user">Email or username</label>
        <input class="bo-input" id="user" name="username" autocomplete="username" required />
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-field">
        <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="pass">Password</label>
        <input class="bo-input" id="pass" name="password" type="password"
            autocomplete="current-password" required />
      </div>
      <div class="bo-form-actions">
        <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Sign in</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import { initValidationSummary } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initValidationSummary(); // client-side empty-field summary; server errors
                            // re-render the same alert box with their message
</script>`}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/components/form", "Forms"],
    ["/patterns/validation-summary", "Validation summary"],
    ["/components/dashboard#card", "Card (.bo-widget)"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
